<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sheba son of Bichri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sheba son of Bichri was a Benjamite who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, led a revolt of the northern tribes of Israel against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> soon after the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/absalom">Absalom</a>. Pursued by David's commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joab">Joab</a> to the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abel-beth-maacah">Abel-beth-maacah</a>, he was beheaded by its inhabitants, who threw his head over the wall to end the siege.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sheba-son-of-bichri.jpg" alt="Sheba son of Bichri" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morgan-bible-fl-46.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
